<title>LUXEMBOURG: CLT-UFA 1996 cons net profit edges up.</title>
<headline>CLT-UFA 1996 cons net profit edges up.</headline>
<dateline>LUXEMBOURG 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year 1996</p>
<p>(in billions of Luxembourg francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit				  3.37    vs 3.34</p>
<p>    Gross dividend/share (francs)		122     vs 120</p>
<p>NOTE - CLT-UFA is a Luxembourg-based broadcaster which was formed in January. CLT was a unit of Belgian-Luxembourg media holding company Audiofina and UFA the television unit of German media concern Bertelsmann. It leads the television market in Germany, the Netherlands and the French-speaking part of Belgium. It is also market leader in French radio and has a strong position in French television.</p>
<p>It has also started up operations in several other European countries including the U.K. and Poland.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
